      "text": "To solve the problem using reasoning, we need to understand what a percentage of a number means. A percentage can be expressed as a fraction or a decimal. Specifically, 20% is the same as $\\frac{20}{100}$ or 0.2 when converted to decimal form. Similarly, 10% is 0.1. The phrase \"20% of 10%\" means 0.2 of a quantity that is 0.1. So we can write the problem as a multiplication of two such fractions: $$0.2 \\times 0.1.$$This is equal to $$\\frac{20 \\times 10 }{100 \\times 100},$$ which simplifies to $$\\frac{0.2 \\times 0.1}{0.002} = \\frac{0.02}{0.002} = \\frac{2}{0.08} = 25.$$So the answer is $\\boxed{25}.$.",
